{#-
Projects one serialized Assistance `PeerReply` (tagged by `state`) into the exact deterministic
compact model-facing text the MCP facade has always emitted. The context is the complete
serialized reply, plus `cause_tag` for a tagged execution-profile refusal whose structured copy
keeps the stable public `code`, and for an `unavailable: host_binding` reply's closed cause
(T15B), whose structured copy keeps its historical fields.

Contract:
- Byte-identical to the retired manual formatter; tests in `src/assistance/content.rs` assert
  exact wording, ordering, references, and the serialized reply budget.
- Every reference must be defined for the state branch that reads it (strict undefined fails
  the render instead of silently dropping a fact): `result.source_ref` is present for every
  success outcome because `EditResult::new` enforces it, `detail_ref` serializes as `null`
  rather than being omitted.
- Untrusted reply text (`text`, `messages`, refs) is bound as data only; it is never
  template source and auto-escaping stays off because the carrier is plain text.
- Whitespace discipline: every block tag carries both trim modifiers and all lines are
  flush-left, so the only newlines in the output are the intentional ones.
-#}
{%- if state == "unavailable" -%}
{%- if reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "invalid_metadata" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (invalid_metadata); the host sent malformed call metadata. Send a new tool call, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "missing_field" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (missing_field); required host call metadata is missing. Send a new tool call, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "invalid_field" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (invalid_field); host call metadata contains an invalid field. Send a new tool call, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "invalid_attachment" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (invalid_attachment); the host attachment does not identify this call. Repeat the call, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "unsupported_hook_phase" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (unsupported_hook_phase); the host reported an unsupported tool-call phase. Repeat the call, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "missing_invocation" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (missing_invocation); the host's completion event arrived before its tool call was validated. Send a new tool call, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "outside_allowed_roots" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (outside_allowed_roots); the session project is outside the directories the IDE may open. Call ide.start with an allowed root, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "hooks_not_delivered" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (hooks_not_delivered); the daemon has received no host event for this session. Call ide.start with the same root, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "missing_pre" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (missing_pre); the host's before-tool event for this call did not reach the daemon. Repeat the call once, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "replay" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (replay); this exact call was already processed. Send it as a new tool call, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "mismatch" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (mismatch); the host event did not match this call. Repeat the call, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "inactive_binding" and tool_name == "ide.test" and test_status_id -%}
unavailable: host_binding (inactive_binding); this session's IDE activation has stopped; read run {{ test_status_id }} with ide.inspect {"detail_ref":"tests #{{ test_status_id }}"}, or call ide.start to run tests again
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "inactive_binding" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (inactive_binding); this session's IDE activation has stopped. Call ide.start, then repeat this call, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "never_activated" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (never_activated); no IDE activation in this session yet. Call ide.start, then repeat this call, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "capacity_exceeded" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (capacity_exceeded); the daemon's session table is full. Call ide.stop, then ide.start, or continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag == "host_unrecognized" -%}
unavailable: host_binding (host_unrecognized); this host did not identify the call in a supported format. Continue with native tools
{%- elif reason == "host_binding" and cause_tag is startingwith("project_moved:") -%}
unavailable: host_binding ({{ cause_tag }}); the IDE could not move to the requested root. Call ide.start under the session's current root, or continue with native tools
{%- else -%}
unavailable: {{ reason }}{% if cause_tag %} ({{ cause_tag }}){% endif %}; continue with native tools
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if state == "hook_observed" -%}
hook_observed: native pre-hook retained
{%- endif -%}
{%- if state == "hook_settled" -%}
hook_settled: validated invocation settled
{%- endif -%}
{%- if state == "native_hook_observed" -%}
native_hook_observed: registered-path reconciliation requested
{%- endif -%}
{%- if state == "feedback" -%}
